Get PM Counters From NetAct
    [Arguments]  ${technology}    ${measurement}   ${counters}   ${filter_by}   ${mo_names}
    ...          ${object_aggregation}   ${time_aggregation}   ${time_filter}   ${time_filter_dict}=${EMPTY}     ${netact_index}=${None}
    [Documentation]  This keyword is used to get PM counters from NetAct. Please refer to the TAF DOC to get the arguments discription.
    ...  https://taf-nms-netact.docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/en/latest/interfaces/interface.html#taf.nms.netact.interface.netact.get_pm_counters
    ...
    ...  *AUTHOR*   calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...  *Examples*
    ...  | ${counters}=  | Get PM Counters From NetAct | technology=SBTS-Nokia Single RAN Base Transceiver Station |
    ...  |               |                             | measurement=Ethernet Link Statistics |
    ...  |               |                             | counters=EthIfInFrames |
    ...  |               |                             | filter_by=PLMN |
    ...  |               |                             | mo_names=PLMN-PLMN |
    ...  |               |                             | object_aggregation=PLMN/SBTS/TNL/ETHSVC/ETHLK |
    ...  |               |                             | time_aggregation=RAW |
    ...  |               |                             | time_filter=today |
    ...  |               |                             | time_filter_dict={'start_time':'xxx', 'end_time':'xxxx'} |
    ${counters}=    netact_ope.get_netact_pm_counters   technology=${technology}    measurement=${measurement}
    ...          counters=${counters}   filter_by=${filter_by}   mo_names=${mo_names}
    ...          object_aggregation=${object_aggregation}   time_aggregation=${time_aggregation}   time_filter=${time_filter}
    ...          time_filter_dict=${time_filter_dict}   netact_index=${netact_index}
    [Return]   ${counters}

Modify Parameter From NetAct
    [Arguments]    ${para_list}   ${activate_plan}=${True}   ${netact_index}=${None}
    [Documentation]  This keyword is used to modify parameters from NetAct.
    ...
    ...   *AUTHOR* calla.wang@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...  - *para_list*: parameters list that need to be updated. e.g,
    ...                 [{'dist_name':'PLMN-PLMN/MRBTS-1', 'p_name':'btsName', 'value':'TEST_BTS', 'operation':'update'},
    ...                  {'dist_name': 'PLMN-PLMN/MRBTS-368961/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/TEST-1', 'operation': 'create'},
    ...                  {'dist_name': 'PLMN-PLMN/MRBTS-368961/MNL-1/MNLENT-1/TEST-1/RFTHLD-1','p_name': 'rfTemperatureHighThreshold','value': '80', 'operation': 'create'},
    ...                  {'dist_name':'PLMN-PLMN/MRBTS-1', 'operation':'delete'}]
    ...  - *activate_plan*: If set to true, provision operation is 'activate'.
    ...                     If set to false, provision operation is 'preactivate'.
    ...  - *netact_index*: NetAct index in testline configurtion file. Default is None.
    ...                    NetAct can be configured as a list in testline configure file. This parameter is used
    ...                    to identify which netact will be used. If it is set to None, the first netact that can be connected
    ...                    by ssh will be selected. Otherwise, the given netact index will be used.

    netact_ope.modify_parameters_via_netact   param_list=${para_list}  activate_plan=${activate_plan}  netact_index=${netact_index}

Check Alarm Existed in Netact Via Alarm ID
    [Arguments]   ${mrbts_name}   ${alarm_id}   ${alarm_type}=active   ${time_start_days}=${7}   ${netact_index}=${None}
    [Documentation]   This keyword is used to Check Active or History Alarm Existed in Netact Via Alarm ID.
    ...
    ...   *AUTHOR* rui.3.li@nokia-sbell.com
    ...
    ...  - *mrbts_name*: mrbts id, like MRBTS-5031.
    ...  - *alarm_id*: alarm id
    ...  - *alarm_id*: alarm type, only support active or history, if not keyword will fail, default is active.
    ...  - *time_start_days*: vaild if alarm_type is history, means start time used to get history alarm.
    ...  - *netact_index*: NetAct index in testline configurtion file. Default is None.
    ...                    NetAct can be configured as a list in testline configure file. This parameter is used
    ...                    to identify which netact will be used. If it is set to None, the first netact that can be connected
    ...                    by ssh will be selected. Otherwise, the given netact index will be used.

    ${all_alarm_list}=   Run Keyword If   '${alarm_type}'=='active'   netact_ope.get_all_alarms  ${mrbts_name}   ${netact_index}
    ...   ELSE IF   '${alarm_type}'=='history'   netact_ope.get_cleared_alarms   ${mrbts_name}   netact_index=${netact_index}   time_start_days=${time_start_days}
    ...   ELSE  Fail  This type of alarm is not currently supported
    FOR  ${alarm}  IN  @{all_alarm_list}
       Return From Keyword If   '${alarm}[alarmKey][alarmId]'=='${alarm_id}'
    END
    ${error_info}   Set Variable    Check Alarm Exist in Netact Via Alarm ID Fail
    Fail   ${error_info}

